url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-04T09:41:38Z","updated_at":"2023-07-04T09:41:38Z","body":"@gstaa No time to review this right now. I'll look into later.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1619909237/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1639193966","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1639193966","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1639193966,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5htB1u","user":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-18T02:38:01Z","updated_at":"2023-07-18T02:38:01Z","body":"@gstaa Are there any standard documentation we can refer to to see if these modifications are possible?","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1639193966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1639536889","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1639536889","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1639536889,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5huVj5","user":{"login":"gstaa","id":93838663,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZfdRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93838663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa","html_url":"https://github.com/gstaa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-18T05:57:56Z","updated_at":"2023-07-18T05:57:56Z","body":"@acetcom I added some explanations to the expected behaviour:\r\n![UPF_HA_IDLE_flow_simple_explained](https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/assets/93838663/b2ee6f34-d82e-48bb-b275-6a4b28ed8160)\r\n\r\n**SMF**:\r\n\r\nETSI TS 123 502 V16.7.0, 4.2.3.2 UE Triggered Service Request\r\n\r\nThe SMF decides to rejects the activation of UP connection of a PDU Session of SSC mode 2, and trigger re-establishment of the PDU Session after Service Request procedure to perform the allocation of a new UPF to act as PDU Session Anchor, e.g. the UE has moved out of the service area of the anchor UPF which is connecting to NG-RAN\r\n\r\nThe SMF can reject the activation of UP of the PDU Session by including a cause in the Nsmf_PDUSession_UpdateSMContext Response\r\n\r\nETSI TS 129 502 V16.12.0, 5.2.2.3.2.2 Activation of User Plane connectivity of a PDU session\r\n\r\nIf the SMF cannot proceed with activating the user plane connection\r\nof the PDU session (e.g. if the PDU session corresponds to a PDU session of SSC mode 2 and the SMF decides to change the PDU Session Anchor), the SMF shall return an error response, as specified for step 2b of figure 5.2.2.3.1-1.  For a 4xx/5xx response, the SmContextUpdateError structure shall include the following additional information:\r\n\r\n- upCnxState attribute set to DEACTIVATED.\r\n\r\nETSI TS 123 502 V16.7.0, 4.2.3.2 UE Triggered Service Request\r\n\r\nIf the SMF decided to change the PSA UPF for the requested PDU Session as described in step 5b.\r\nIn this case, after sending Nsmf_PDUSession_UpdateSMContext Response, the SMF\r\ntriggers another procedure to instruct UE to re-establish the PDU Session as described in clause 4.3.5.1 for SSC mode 2.\r\n\r\n**AMF**:\r\n\r\nETSI TS 124 501 V16.5.1, 5.6.1.4 Service request procedure accepted by the network\r\n\r\nIf the user-plane resources cannot be established for a PDU session, the AMF shall include the PDU session reactivation\r\nresult IE in the SERVICE ACCEPT message indicating that user-plane resources for the corresponding PDU session\r\ncannot be re-established, and:\r\n- if the user-plane resources cannot be established because the SMF indicated to the AMF that the resource is not available in the UPF (see 3GPP TS 29.502 [20A]), the AMF shall include the PDU session reactivation result error cause IE with the 5GMM cause set to 92 \"insufficient user-plane resources for the PDU session\";\r\n\r\nNOTE: It is up to UE implementation when to re-send a request for user-plane re-establishment for the associated PDU session after receiving a PDU session reactivation result error cause IE with a 5GMM cause set to\r\n92 \"insufficient user-plane resources for the PDU session\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1639536889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1640298276","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1640298276","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1640298276,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5hxPck","user":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-18T14:06:36Z","updated_at":"2023-07-18T14:06:36Z","body":"@gstaa \r\n\r\nIt seems to me that this should be implemented according to standard documentation like below.\r\n\r\n```\r\n- trigger re-establishment of PDU Session. After Service Request procedure,\r\n  SMF sends N1 SM message to the UE via the AMF by invoking \r\n  Namf_Communication_N1N2MessageTransfer containing the cause\r\n  indicating PDU Session re-establishment is required for the UE; or\r\n- keep the PDU Session, but reject the activation request of User Plane connection\r\n  for the PDU Session and inform the AMF about it; or\r\n- release the PDU Session after Service Request procedure.\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'm not sure that #2418 is implemented properly, so it won't be merged.\r\n\r\nSorry for not help this.\r\nSukchan","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1640298276/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1645119283","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1645119283","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1645119283,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5iDocz","user":{"login":"gstaa","id":93838663,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZfdRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93838663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa","html_url":"https://github.com/gstaa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-21T07:33:49Z","updated_at":"2023-07-21T07:35:05Z","body":"@acetcom I agree this flow better follows the standards.\r\n\r\nExpected behaviour is therefore:\r\n\r\n![UPF_HA_IDLE_flow_simple_2](https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/assets/93838663/efdf2a30-36e1-4ec8-b56c-d6d18d0ce2f5)\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1645119283/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1649870857","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1649870857","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1649870857,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5iVwgJ","user":{"login":"acetcom","id":4222492,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMjI0OTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4222492?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom","html_url":"https://github.com/acetcom","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acetcom/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T13:41:33Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T13:41:33Z","body":"@gstaa \r\n\r\nI would like to solve this problem by making a small change to the method you suggested.\r\n\r\nSee #2471 for more information, and please let me know if you have any different idea.\r\n\r\nThank you for your contribution.\r\nSukchan\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1649870857/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1669394050","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1669394050","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1669394050,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5jgO6C","user":{"login":"gstaa","id":93838663,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZfdRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93838663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa","html_url":"https://github.com/gstaa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-08T10:56:52Z","updated_at":"2023-08-08T10:56:52Z","body":"@acetcom\r\nThank you, the solution is optimal.\r\n\r\nI only have two minor things to discuss:\r\n\r\n- why does SMF include the n2InfoContainer in namf_Communication_N1N2MessageTransfer?\r\n  N2 has already been released when entering IDLE. SMF gets upCnxState DEACTIVATED, so it is aware of IDLE state. Why does SMF send PDUSessionResourceReleaseCommandTransfer?\r\n- UPF crash is an UPF error, but I believe that the failed activation is not an ERROR on AMF and SMF – it is an expected and supported situation (so INFO, or WARNING):\r\n```\r\n[smf] ERROR: [imsi-001010000000000:1] Service-Request: ACTIVATING FAILED (../src/smf/nsmf-handler.c)\r\n[amf] ERROR: Service-Request: ACTIVATING FAILED [403:DEACTIVATED:PDU_SESSION_ANCHOR_CHANGE] (../src/amf/nsmf-handler)\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1669394050/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1718664609","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1718664609","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1718664609,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5mcL2h","user":{"login":"hcbwiz","id":34223318,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjIzMzE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34223318?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz","html_url":"https://github.com/hcbwiz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-14T02:41:26Z","updated_at":"2023-09-14T02:41:26Z","body":"@gstaa\r\n Could you please share how to configure that \"2 UPFs associate with SMF\" to support UPF HA?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1718664609/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1718806174","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1718806174","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1718806174,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5mcuae","user":{"login":"gstaa","id":93838663,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZfdRw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93838663?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa","html_url":"https://github.com/gstaa","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gstaa/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-09-14T05:54:56Z","updated_at":"2023-09-14T05:54:56Z","body":"@hcbwiz\r\nShould be something like this:\r\n- add second UPF to SMF configuration:\r\n```\r\nmodified   configs/open5gs/smf.yaml.in\r\n@@ -809,6 +809,7 @@ scp:\r\nupf:\r\n     pfcp:\r\n       - addr: 127.0.0.7\r\n+      - addr: 127.0.0.8\r\n```\r\n- copy configs/open5gs/upf.yaml into configs/open5gs/upf2.yaml\r\n- substitute 127.0.0.7 with 127.0.0.8 in configs/open5gs/upf2.yaml\r\n- run both UPF's separately:\r\n```\r\nsrc/upf/open5gs-upfd -c ./configs/open5gs/upf.yaml\r\nsrc/upf/open5gs-upfd -c ./configs/open5gs/upf2.yaml\r\n```\r\nWe use a different environment so I couldn't tested this idea. I hope it helps...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1718806174/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/comments/1719135119","html_url":"https://github.com/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396#issuecomment-1719135119","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/open5gs/open5gs/issues/2396","id":1719135119,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBM4HkM5md-uP","user":{"login":"hcbwiz","id":34223318,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM0MjIzMzE4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/34223318?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz","html_url":"https://github.com/hcbwiz","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hcbwiz/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/us